-- title:
--   Special-fibre n-torsion is finite and bounded by generic torsion
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\mathbb Q$, let $q$ be a prime, and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, with the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$ of characteristic $q$ and $q \nmid N$. Write $J_0(N)$ for `JZero N`, the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field `modularFunctionFieldBar N` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (degree-zero divisors, i.e. finitely supported $\mathbb Z$-valued functions on the places, modulo principal divisors), and write $\mathrm{Pic}^0_{\kappa_A}$ for the same construction over $\kappa_A$ applied to `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\,N$, the $\kappa_A$-subfield of the Laurent series field over $\kappa_A$ generated by the reductions of $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$. Both groups are assumed to carry module structures over the Hecke algebra `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb Z[x_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$. Let $D$ be a good-reduction specialisation datum `JZeroGoodReductionSpecialization A q hq N`: a surjective additive map $\mathrm{sp} : J_0(N) \to \mathrm{Pic}^0_{\kappa_A}$ together with an endomorphism $F$ of $\mathrm{Pic}^0_{\kappa_A}$, such that $\mathrm{sp}$ is Hecke-equivariant, invariant under the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$, intertwines any Frobenius element at $q$ with $F$, is injective on $p$-power torsion for every prime $p \neq q$, and $F$ satisfies the special-fibre relation $F^2 y - x_q\!\cdot\! F y + q y = 0$. Finally let $n > 0$ with $q \nmid n$. The conclusion is that the subgroup $\{c \in \mathrm{Pic}^0_{\kappa_A} : n c = 0\}$ is finite and that its cardinality is at most that of $\{y \in J_0(N) : n y = 0\}$.
--
--   This is the torsion-counting half of the good-reduction comparison between $J_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the reduced modular curve at a prime $q$ not dividing the level, in the style of Serre–Tate. It is used to upgrade surjectivity of the specialisation map on prime-to-$q$ torsion to a bijection, in [`ModularCurve.JZeroGoodReductionSpecialization.torsBijFor_of_charP_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroGoodReductionSpecialization.torsBijFor_of_charP_of_not_dvd).
